# extdir scheduled work.
#
# APPEND these lines to the existing crontab — never `crontab deploy/cron/crontab`.
# That form replaces the whole crontab, and this account also schedules work for
# other sites. Installing this file the obvious way would silently delete them:
#
#   (crontab -l; cat deploy/cron/crontab) | crontab -
#
# Paths are written out in full and the interpreter is /usr/bin/php83, because cron
# runs with a minimal PATH where `php` is either missing or an older default.
#
# Note the absence of a directory variable. cron does not expand variables inside a
# variable assignment: `EXTDIR=$HOME/websites/extdir.com` stores the literal text
# `$HOME/...`, the shell then expands $EXTDIR to that literal, and cd receives a path
# with a `$HOME` in it that nothing will ever resolve. $HOME used directly in a
# command is fine — cron sets HOME and the shell expands it at run time.
#
# Times are deliberately off-peak and staggered. Packagist and GitHub are being
# asked for a few hundred requests; doing that politely costs nothing and being
# rate-limited costs a day of freshness.

# Monitoring: nothing to add here, deliberately.
#
# The usual way to watch a cron job is a heartbeat — the job pings a URL when it
# finishes, and the monitor alerts when the ping stops. UptimeRobot sells that only
# on a paid tier, so instead the app answers the same question at
# https://extdir.com/health/crawl, which returns 503 once the last completed crawl
# is more than 26 hours old. Point an ordinary HTTP(s) monitor at it; every plan
# has those.
#
# The pull version is the better one regardless of price. A heartbeat proves a
# command exited, and a crawl that ran, failed and still exited 0 would satisfy it.
# /health/crawl reads the catalogue's own last_crawled_at, so it proves the data
# actually got fresher — and it keeps working when the server cannot reach the
# internet, which is one of the failure modes worth catching.
#
# /health stays the separate, slower check: it tolerates 48 hours, because "a night
# was missed" and "this data is no longer trustworthy" are different alerts.

# Shopware release timeline. Rarely changes, but everything downstream depends on
# it: the compatibility matrix columns and every maintenance status are measured
# against these dates.
17 3 * * 1   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:shopware:sync-versions >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Package metadata from Packagist. Cheap and the primary source of truth.
23 3 * * *   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:ingest:packagist >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Extensions published to GitHub but never to Packagist. Weekly is enough — a
# repository that was never submitted to Packagist is not moving fast.
41 4 * * 2   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:ingest:github >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Repository signals, then maintenance status and ranking. Must follow ingestion,
# so it runs well after it rather than in parallel.
11 5 * * *   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:signals:refresh >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Download locations. Needs the licence status that enrichment has just settled,
# since an unlicensed extension is never offered a maintainer archive.
47 5 * * *   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:distribution:resolve >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Extension icons: confirm each one still exists where its metadata claims.
#
# Weekly, not nightly. Only a tenth of icon paths are declared in composer.json —
# the rest are the conventional src/Resources/config/plugin.png filled in by the
# extractor, and about a quarter of those point at nothing. The command re-checks
# an icon roughly monthly, so a weekly run spreads the work without ever leaving a
# renamed repository advertised for long. Must follow enrichment: it needs the
# default branch the signals refresh records.
#
# Runs after the catalogue is otherwise settled because it is the slowest job per
# request served — a HEAD to a few hundred forges, about two minutes.
29 6 * * 3   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:ui:verify-icons >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Categories, recomputed from stored data. Seconds, no network.
13 6 * * *   cd $HOME/websites/extdir.com && /usr/bin/php83 bin/console app:taxonomy:classify >> $HOME/logs/extdir-cron.log 2>&1

# Database backup, kept for 14 days.
30 2 * * *   $HOME/websites/extdir.com/deploy/backup.sh >> $HOME/logs/extdir-backup.log 2>&1
